# Comms-channel acknowledgements for every drone drill gate, automatic or
# fallback. Design principle (source_index.md section 8): every microachievement
# gets a Comms confirmation, not just the current-objective (blue text) update -
# see the proven pattern in act1_generator_tarsis_gate.mast's Kestrel/Tarsis
# handlers, every one of which pairs a comms_receive with any objective change.
shared drone_01_scan_confirmed_text = "Artemis - Science: Scan confirmed. Drone 01 reads as a TSN training contact."
shared drone_01_shield_relay_confirmed_text = "Artemis - Science: Weak shield frequency relayed to Weapons."
shared drone_01_weapons_lock_next_step_text = "Artemis - Weapons: Lock beams on Drone 01.\nArtemis - Helm: Bring us between 1 and 2 kilometres and hold stationary for fifteen seconds."
# Beam lock is where the manual-targeting technique gets taught: Weapons is already
# on the console, and the crew still has range and stationary hold to fly before
# clearance, so there is time to read it. Deliberately NOT in the fire-clearance
# message - that one stays a short Captain's order (see the note above
# drone_01_weapons_crit_technique_text).
#
# Every claim here is checked against legendarymissions/consoles/manual_weapons.mast:
#   - "keep pressing the same subsystem button" - the 1-in-20 roll is per PRESS
#     (line 187), with no cooldown, and `yield idle if critical` (line 180) makes
#     presses after a success no-ops rather than re-rolls.
#   - "the console flashes it in yellow" - line 190, stock output, not ours.
#   - "your next beam hit delivers it" - the //damage/object route at line 196
#     consumes the armed critical; it cannot land without a beam actually hitting.
#   - "more critical hits per minute" - THROUGHPUT, not odds. Fire rate is not a
#     term in the roll, but delivery requires a landed hit, so once a crew is
#     mashing fast enough to stay armed between shots, crits-per-minute tracks
#     hits-per-minute. Do not reword this into "more chances at a critical".
#   - "straight through her shields" - operator-validated live 2026-08-16. A
#     critical bypasses shields and lands on the named subsystem directly; the crew
#     does NOT have to strip shields first. This overturned three comments in this
#     file that asserted the opposite - see the hull-hold note below.
#   - "weapons, engine and sensor" - those are the only three buttons the console
#     builds (manual_weapons.mast:136-144). There is deliberately no shields button,
#     so do not write "all her subsystems" and send the crew hunting for one.
#   - "inside 2 km" - manual_weapons.mast:108, `jump manual_weapons_minimize if
#     dist > 2000`. Conveniently the same band Helm is already holding for the drill.
#
# ASCII only, and " - " rather than an em dash: every player-facing string in
# scripts/ is pure ASCII, and nothing proves the game client renders a non-ASCII
# character correctly in a comms message.
shared drone_01_weapons_lock_confirmed_text = "Artemis - Weapons: Beam lock confirmed on Drone 01.\nArtemis - Weapons: Press Manual, lower left. Inside 2 km her weapons, engine and sensor buttons appear. Press the same one until the console flashes \"Potential Critical hit\" in yellow. Your next beam carries it straight through her shields.\nArtemis - Weapons: Never switch subsystems while one is armed or your critical hit will reset. Also note that a faster (4X vs. 1X) beam rate delivers more critical hits per minute.\nArtemis - Science: Pass Weapons the weak shield frequency. While the critical hit punches through on its own, switching standard beam hits to the enemy's weakest shield frequency can take down their shields much quicker."
shared drone_01_range_confirmed_text = "Artemis - Helm: Range confirmed, one to two kilometres from Drone 01."
shared drone_01_stationary_hold_confirmed_text = "Artemis - Helm: Stationary hold confirmed."
shared drone_01_fire_authorized_confirmed_text = "Artemis - Captain: Fire clearance issued for the controlled disable."
shared drone_01_weapons_disabled_confirmed_text = "Artemis - Weapons: Drone 01's weapons array is disabled. Stop firing."
# The ceasefire line is also the handoff to Drone 02. Before this was spelled out,
# Drone 01 was simply deleted the moment ceasefire was confirmed and a second
# contact appeared with no explanation - the operator read the vanish as "we were
# supposed to destroy it." Say plainly that Drone 01 is recovered rather than
# killed, why that is the lesson, and that the next contact IS a kill.
shared drone_01_ceasefire_confirmed_text = "Artemis - Weapons: Ceasefire confirmed. Drone 01 is disabled, not destroyed. Taking a system instead of a ship is the whole point of that drill.\nArtemis - Comms: Kestrel is pulling Drone 01 off the range now.\nArtemis - Captain: Stand by for a second drone. That one is a live-fire target, and you will destroy it."
shared drone_02_destroyed_confirmed_text = "Artemis - Weapons: Drone 02 destroyed."
# Drone 02 fights back, unlike Drone 01. Warn the crew before it opens fire - the
# whole point is pressure, not ambush, and this is the first time in the mission
# anything shoots at them.
shared drone_02_hostile_warning_text = "Artemis - Captain: Weapons free on Drone 02. Be aware this one is not passive, it will manoeuvre and return fire.\nArtemis - Engineering: Shields up and keep an eye on your damage. This is where the DAMCON work from the shakedown earns its keep."
# Science keeps the tactical picture live. The Captain's fire-clearance message
# stays deliberately concise: it states the disable-only order and names the
# report-back gate instead of narrating the stock console's critical-hit
# implementation.
#
# CORRECTED 2026-08-16 (operator-validated live): this line previously ended
# "manual targeting cannot reach a subsystem through an intact shield", which is
# false - a critical bypasses shields entirely. That wording told the crew to wait
# for something they never needed to wait for. Shield levels are still worth
# calling because ordinary beam damage does go through the shields first, and
# because frequency matching is what brings them down, but they gate nothing.
# CORRECTED 2026-08-16 (operator-validated live, second correction to this line):
# this previously said "Scan her again after every hit", which does not work.
# Re-pressing a band that has already been scanned returns the engine's cache and
# changes nothing - the operator watched WEAP sit at 100% through repeated presses
# of the status band while the engine reported system_damage 0.86 of 2.0. What DOES
# refresh the figures is scanning a band that has not been scanned yet: intel or
# bio re-resolved the subsystem numbers immediately, and neither of those bands
# carries subsystem data, so the refresh is bound to a scan COMPLETING rather than
# to which band ran.
#
# The old wording therefore sent Science to do the one thing that provably fails.
# The wording below states the measured limitation directly: a scan offers one
# clean read, so the crew must spend its available scans deliberately.
shared drone_01_science_report_request_text = "Artemis - Science: Her shield levels read live on your panel, so call them out as they come down.\nArtemis - Science: Subsystem integrity is not updated in real time as the enemy ship will only allow you to get a single clean read. If you scan the intel or bio bands, it will update your target's sub-system damage, but only once per scan. Plan your scans well to balance your intel gathering with any sub-system visibility you may need in combat.\nArtemis - Science: A critical hit reaches the subsystem whether her shields are up or not, so do not hold Weapons back waiting on them."
shared drone_01_weapons_crit_technique_text = "Artemis - Captain: Order your ship into battle and disable, but do not destroy, the drone. After success, report back to Commander Dillon at Kestrel Yards."
shared drone_01_known_marked = False
